# A Guided Tour of Strange Loops

Begin with the central distinction: **truth** is semantic, while **provability** is internal to a system. A sound system satisfies $P(s)\Rightarrow T(s)$, but the converse need not hold. For historical context, see the [Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy entry on Gödel](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/goedel-incompleteness/) and its discussion of [Tarski's truth definitions](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/tarski-truth/).

