<details><summary>Reveal why truth is also undefinable</summary>
If one code represented semantic truth, closure of represented predicates under negation would turn its negated code into a representation of semantic untruth. The liar obstruction forbids the latter, so it forbids the former. This concerns a uniform same-level truth predicate, not truth predicates for a lower language in a stratified hierarchy.
</details>

## When hierarchies close into cycles

Truth-preserving, proof-reflecting interpretations carry true-but-unprovable sentences forward. Two opposite interpretations create a cycle with a native and an imported witness on each level.

